<span class="c-p">-</span> <span class="c-k">name</span><span class="c-p">:</span> <span class="c-s">annotate1</span>
  <span class="c-k">title</span><span class="c-p">:</span> <span class="c-s">Kandinsky composition</span>
  <span class="c-k">position</span><span class="c-p">:</span> <span class="c-p">[</span><span class="c-n">-220</span><span class="c-p">, </span><span class="c-n">-190</span><span class="c-p">]</span>
  <span class="c-k">size</span><span class="c-p">:</span> <span class="c-p">[</span><span class="c-n">820</span><span class="c-p">, </span><span class="c-n">450</span><span class="c-p">]</span></code></pre>

      <ul class="tdn__bullets">
        <li><strong>this is the file behind the frames above</strong> &mdash; the real export, trimmed to fit. The three frames are three versions of it.</li>
        <li><strong>non-default-only</strong> &mdash; only what you actually changed gets written.</li>
        <li><strong>type defaults hoisted</strong> &mdash; shared properties dedupe across operators.</li>
        <li><strong>expression shorthand</strong> &mdash; <code>=parent.Kandinsky.par.Seed</code> instead of a wrapper object.</li>
        <li><strong>round-trip safe</strong> &mdash; export &rarr; edit &rarr; import yields the same network.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="tdn__link">
      <a href="https://dylanroscover.github.io/Embody/tdxn/specification/">read the full TDXN specification <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
